WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Why Donald Trump will deport Ilhan Omar

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.700
Donald Trump warned America long ago that one day,

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.800
the truth about Ilhan Omar would come crashing down like a hammer.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.340
And now, with Trump back in charge and the emperor finally seated on his throne again,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.900
the crackdown on immigration fraud is no longer a threat.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:22.380
It's a reality.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:27.800
And Ilhan Omar, well, she might want to start packing before the music stops.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:35.020
For years, Omar moved through Washington like someone who believed the law was a suggestion, not a requirement.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:43.120
Fake identities, suspicious paperwork, a marriage that investigators say looked more like a family reunion than a wedding.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:49.000
Her story reads like one of those immigration cases Trump loves to expose on stage.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:06.580
And now that he's tightening the net on fake citizenships, fraudulent asylum claims, and people who enter the U.S. using children who are not even theirs, Ilhan Omar stands exactly where she never wanted to be, directly in Trump's spotlight.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:20.420
Under Trump's renewed immigration crackdown, federal agencies are going back through old naturalization files, line by line, date by date, looking for lies or omissions.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:25.680
And according to investigators, Omar's file may as well be glowing red.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:34.820
Years of allegations that she lied on documents, used a false name, and married her own brother to help him enter the country illegally.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.960
Suddenly, those accusations are no longer political gossip.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:47.100
Under Trump, they are grounds for denaturalization, and denaturalization is grounds for deportation.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:53.500
Trump officials have already removed U.S. citizenship from criminals, fraudsters, gang members,

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.580
and even people who lied about something as small as their marital status.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:03.720
So what happens when one of the most controversial members of Congress is accused of doing far worse?

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.180
Trump's DOJ calls that priority

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:10.600
What makes Omar's case even more explosive

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:16.040
Is the way some Somali immigrants brought the same ideology that tore apart their own country

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.660
Somalia is peaceful enough today that thousands travel back and forth

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.960
Build houses, buy land, and visit family

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:28.360
If it's safe for vacations, weddings, and business deals

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.940
Then why are some of them still claiming the U.S. must shelter them from danger?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.620
And worse, why do some bring the same corrupt political games,

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:43.740
same clan loyalty, same chaos, and same identity fraud that ruined their homeland,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.680
only to repeat it in America?

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.940
Trump has asked that question more times than anyone else in Washington,

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.720
and now he's acting on it.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:55.960
Under his leadership, fraud rings that used fake disabled children

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:58.840
to extort U.S. taxpayers are being dismantled.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:03.640
Family networks that swap identities like raffle tickets are being exposed.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.700
And Omar, with her suspicious timelines, mismatched.
